    {
      "id": "44116098",
      "title": "Angular Modules (NgModule) & Dependency Injection",
      "lectureOrder": 191,
      "videoOrder": 183,
      "sourceHash": "5cea86b13ef0f504724f44e5b6515b05dc928fc37336b68f05e0c7218b4c26ca",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.99,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "So now that we had a very close look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 7.92,
          "en": "and a pretty deep dive into services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.92,
          "end": 9.615,
          "en": "and dependency injection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.615,
          "end": 14.615,
          "en": "it's worth noting that you can use all these features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.06,
          "end": 16.623,
          "en": "and concepts you learn about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.623,
          "end": 20.46,
          "en": "not just with standalone component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.46,
          "end": 24.061,
          "en": "which is what we used in this project thus far,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.061,
          "end": 26.49,
          "en": "but also with modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.49,
          "end": 30.003,
          "en": "when creating Angular modules with NgModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.71,
          "end": 34.68,
          "en": "In that case, you would create those modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.68,
          "end": 36.87,
          "en": "as you learned it before in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.87,
          "end": 39.21,
          "en": "You would declare your components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.21,
          "end": 42.36,
          "en": "import any other modules you might need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.36,
          "end": 45.93,
          "en": "and you also have a provider's array there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.93,
          "end": 50.93,
          "en": "which you can set up, because when using modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.18,
          "end": 54.36,
          "en": "then in the main.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.36,
          "end": 58.74,
          "en": "you start your application by calling bootstrapModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.74,
          "end": 63.36,
          "en": "on this platform browser dynamic thing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.36,
          "end": 68.36,
          "en": "And bootstrapModule then takes the app module as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.78999999999999,
          "end": 72.359,
          "en": "And you can then use this providers array here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.359,
          "end": 76.643,
          "en": "on this module to register providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.643,
          "end": 79.98,
          "en": "with that module injector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.98,
          "end": 82.05,
          "en": "which works essentially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.05,
          "end": 86.25,
          "en": "like the Application root Environmentinjector here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 86.25,
          "end": 89.811,
          "en": "since it will make whatever you are providing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.811,
          "end": 93.06,
          "en": "available to your entire application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.06,
          "end": 98.06,
          "en": "Since this is the root app module of the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.16,
          "end": 101.67,
          "en": "You could also pass a configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 101.67,
          "end": 105.15,
          "en": "as a second argument to bootstrap module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.15,
          "end": 108.39,
          "en": "and there, set up some providers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.39,
          "end": 113.28,
          "en": "but it is a bit more common to do that in the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 116.13,
          "en": "Now, if you would be using multiple modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 116.13,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "you could also add providers to your nested modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 121.44,
          "en": "but behind the scenes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.44,
          "end": 126.44,
          "en": "they would all be merged together into one module injector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 127.14,
          "end": 130.41,
          "en": "unless you load nested modules lazily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 130.41,
          "end": 132.84,
          "en": "but that's a more advanced technique",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 132.84,
          "end": 135.99,
          "en": "to which I'll get back later in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.99,
          "end": 138.78,
          "en": "But in general, when you work with modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 138.78,
          "end": 140.835,
          "en": "no matter if it's just one module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 140.835,
          "end": 145.47,
          "en": "or multiple modules, you can register values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 145.47,
          "end": 149.94,
          "en": "you can provide values with this providers array here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 149.94,
          "end": 152.46,
          "en": "and if you're working with multiple modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.46,
          "end": 155.017,
          "en": "they will be merged together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 155.017,
          "end": 158.7,
          "en": "And everything else works just the way you learned it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 158.7,
          "end": 160.617,
          "en": "You can still use custom tokens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.617,
          "end": 163.60399999999998,
          "en": "you can use the more common shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 163.60399999999998,
          "end": 166.65,
          "en": "so that if you're injecting a service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 166.65,
          "end": 169.38,
          "en": "you are just providing it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.38,
          "end": 173.67000000000002,
          "en": "That would also work if you don't want a custom token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 175.59,
          "en": "so that all won't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.59,
          "end": 178.65,
          "en": "It's just that extra module injector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 178.65,
          "end": 180.87,
          "en": "with which you can now register",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.87,
          "end": 183.723,
          "en": "your injectable services and values.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
